nt": "token", "delta": "### Hyperconductivity Evaluation (test fixture)\n\nNo, ambient hyperconductivity has **not** been confirmed in synthetic phospho-silicate matrices.\n\nWhile an initial preprint asserted zero electrical resistance above 380 K [[c:0]], independent multi-center crystallographic replications refuting the phenomenon established that ferromagnetic domain pinning of nickel impurities caused the observed measurement artifacts [[c:1]]."}\n\ndata: {"event": "audit", "answer_final": "### Hyperconductivity Evaluation (test fixture)\n\nNo, ambient hyperconductivity has **not** been confirmed in synthetic phospho-silicate matrices.\n\nWhile an initial preprint asserted zero electrical resistance above 380 K [[c:0]], independent multi-center crystallographic replications refuting the phenomenon established that ferromagnetic domain pinning of nickel impurities caused the observed measurement artifacts [[c:1]].", "confidence": 0.38, "tier_agreement": "conflicting", "claims": [{"claim_id": 0, "text": "No, ambient hyperconductivity has not been confirmed in synthetic phospho-silicate matrices.", "status": "supported", "citation_ids": [1], "supported": true, "evidence": "Independent replications confirm that anomalous resistance transitions originate exclusively from ferromagnetic domain pinning of nickel impurities rather than superconductivity (test fixture).", "start": 46, "end": 140}, {"claim_id": 1, "text": "While an initial preprint asserted zero electrical resistance above 380 K, independent multi-center crystallographic replications refuting the phenomenon established that ferromagnetic domain pinning of nickel impurities caused the observed measurement artifacts.", "status": "unsupported", "citation_ids": [0], "supported": false, "evidence": "Refuted by independent crystallographic replications (test fixture).", "note": "Citation [[c:0]] flagged in Retraction Watch DB for unverified measurement artifacts (test fixture).", "start": 143, "end": 422}], "c